**Search and rejection summary**
- I screened roughly 30 documents across World Bank Iran monitors, IMF country and working-paper material, Reuters/Euronews reporting, World Bank data tables, and Iranian/Persian-language policy reproductions.
- I kept the World Bank April 2022 and Spring 2022 Iran monitors because they give the strongest 2022 macro baseline, jobs, inflation, and welfare context.
- I kept the IMF inflation paper because it is the clearest Iran-specific analytical source on why inflation was high and what reforms would matter.
- I kept the World Bank MENA labor-market report because it gives the cleanest statement on state-owned enterprises, preferential treatment, and the private-sector level-playing-field problem.
- I kept the Reuters budget, bread-price, currency, and central-bank stories because they provide concrete 2022 policy actions and household effects.
- I kept the World Bank DataBank Gini table because it gives a direct 2022 inequality datapoint.
- I kept the Persian-language seventh-plan decree reproduction because it is the best local-language evidence for Khamenei's stated economic priorities in 2022.
- I rejected or collapsed multiple duplicates of the same March 2022 Khamenei speech, multiple syndicated copies of the bread-subsidy and currency stories, and general IMF methodology pages that did not add Iran-specific evidence.
- I also set aside later 2024-2025 poverty briefs and 2026 war-era news because they were out of period for the 2022 chapter, even when they were informative about longer-run trends.
- I did not keep older 2017-2021 IMF financial-sector papers as target-year evidence; they remain useful only as inherited-baseline background, not 2022 ruler-period proof.

**Remaining gaps**
- Direct ruler-attributed evidence on economic appointments is still thin. The record shows a cabinet-level central-bank reshuffle and general policy direction, but not a clean Khamenei-specific personnel choice in 2022.
- Household welfare is better evidenced than ruler attribution, but a stronger 2022 poverty micro-series for Iran would help, especially for regional and gender distribution.
- Evidence on anti-corruption, monopoly power, and bonyad/IRGC-linked capture under Khamenei in 2022 is still mostly structural rather than ruler-specific.
- The strongest missing piece for a higher-confidence judgment is implementation evidence: whether the 7th development-plan targets, tax-financing shift, and productive-credit directives were actually carried out in 2022 rather than remaining slogans.
- More search would help, especially in Persian, if you want to tighten 5B.2 and 5B.5 rather than relying on macro context plus ruler rhetoric.

